From 7fdf1529bd7f1097000f68227054c5fc7860d0c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 13:54:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [DOSKUTSU] patch 0307 -- fix the two structural faults in
 0298's drum envelopes

0298 authored per-slot drum envelopes from the OPL3 register semantics and
said in its own message that nobody had heard them, that EAR was the gate,
and that the table should be revised rather than the mechanism reverted.
Round F's EAR cell heard them on BOTH OPL3 and AdLib: clipped cymbal and
blip sounds, with the note placement correct. Mechanism right, constants
wrong -- the outcome 0298 predicted.

Two faults, and 0298 inherited both unchanged from the single PATCH_DRUM it
replaced, which is why it still sounds like that burst in eight lengths.

SL=0 on every operator meant the decay phase's target equalled the peak, so
decay terminated immediately and DR never ran. The six differentiated DR
values 0298 carefully chose provably did nothing; the audible tail was RR
alone. SL=15 makes decay traverse the full range at DR as authored. Each
patch keeps its original RR in the low nibble, so the open/closed hat
distinction built with RR 6 vs 15 survives and the DR distinction begins to
work.

Modulator TL=0 pinned FM depth at maximum. With modulator MULT at 14-15 on
the noisy entries that is deep high-ratio FM, which produces dense
inharmonic sidebands -- the clang the operator described. Now attenuated per
drum, more for the pitched entries than the noisy ones. Carrier TL stays 0;
that is the drum's output level and it was already correct.

Only bytes 1, 3 and 9 change in each table. Bytes 0, 2, 4, 5, 6, 8, 10 and
11 are untouched, so every MULT, AR, DR, RR, WS and FB/CONN value 0298 chose
is preserved.

The first fault is structural and provable. The second's eight replacement
values are reasoned from the register semantics and NOT heard, which is
exactly what 0298 did -- they are a second pass and should be expected to
need revision. EAR remains the gate. Shipping this ahead of that audition is
still an improvement, because the SL fix is correct independently of taste.

Data-only: no code path is touched, so this cannot move dc_ms, flip_inner or
the engine bucket. The OPL2 copy is byte-identical to the OPL3 one, matching
how that file already carries its own copies of every PATCH_* constant. The
pre-existing WS=7 note on the OPL2 path is left alone -- a real OPL2 masks
waveforms above 3, which is an AdLib-only timbre question and cannot explain
the OPL3 result.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/sound/MidiBackendOpl2.cpp | 42 ++++++++++++++++++++-----
 src/sound/MidiBackendOpl3.cpp | 58 +++++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 2 files changed, 76 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)

